                  {
                    "value": "Why there is no denial-risk model here.  ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "9pt",
                      "color": "#8FA9AD",
                      "fontWeight": "bold"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "Patient age, claim size, line count and days-to-submit all correlate with denial at |r| < 0.01. A model on them would fit noise, then hold up claims that were never at risk. 23 of 500 providers sit beyond two standard errors - 4.6%, against the 4.55% chance predicts - and the worst is z = 3.3, about the maximum 500 draws give. The only real effect is Self Pay, 2.95% against 8.79%.",
